# tally 2.1.8 R16 (#175, p6noinst), L §4.6, §8.4: a reading after m where m doesn't exist (a false when) is
# RUN-RECORD, from m's point on: konto on the 10th reads as before, from the 18th each read is refused, and so is
# last. 2.1.7 dropped the reading in silence.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input keep: money PLN
input d_save: date
input go: bool

move save: transfers
  on d_save
  reads konto
  when go
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

move mm[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1 day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d_save = 2026-03-18 "s"
  go = false "s"
  opening[konto] = 1050.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..2026-05
  known 2026-01-02
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 90.00 PLN after save "saldo"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-10), bal(konto, 2026-03-20), bal(konto, 2026-04-20), bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
ask g: last(stated[konto], 2026-05-31)
=== expect
b: (1 050.00 PLN, refused: RUN-RECORD reading stated[konto] after save: save doesn't exist, refused: RUN-RECORD reading stated[konto] after save: save doesn't exist, refused: RUN-RECORD reading stated[konto] after save: save doesn't exist)
  cut 2026-06-10
g: refused: RUN-RECORD reading stated[konto] after save: save doesn't exist
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
